const e="sardar-patel-university-youth-festival",d=2026,t="Read in full: the 12-page Sardar Patel University Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival Handbook 2026-27 (rules as formulated and amended by the Association of Indian Universities). Not printed in the source: festival dates, venue, a registration deadline, how or where entries are submitted, entry fees, contact names, phone numbers or addresses, or marks per judging factor. The two trophy rules print donor names for the running trophies; only the trophy roles are kept here. Handbook inconsistencies kept as printed: the events table gives Folk Orchestra 9 participants but the item rule says up to 12; the events table prints minimum times (8 min for Folk/Tribal Dance, 12 min for Classical Dance, 4 min for Elocution, Debate, Mime and Mimicry, 25 min for One Act Play, 8 min for Skits) that the item rules do not repeat; the Cartooning rule on materials is cut off. The Fine Arts table prints 2 hours as the minimum and 2 hours 30 minutes as the maximum. The template's Open Individual and Open Team groups (17 to 24) are a working band: the handbook prints only 'below 25 on 1 July' and no minimum age, so no age group row is written and the age rule is in Page eligibility.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Sardar Patel University Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival 2026-27. Read these rules before you register.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Each college or P.G. department may send only one entry in each item. Only full-time students below 25 years of age on 1 July of the academic year of the festival can take part. Bring an identity card with a photograph.",Notes:["The items, their timings and the number of participants and accompanists are the same for all zones and for the National Youth Festival.","Winning a place here does not by itself give a place in the university team for the inter-university competition."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["These rules are the Handbook of Rules and Regulations of the Sardar Patel University Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival, as formulated and amended by the Association of Indian Universities (AIU), New Delhi.","The festival has 25 competitive items in five families: Music (9), Dance (3), Literary Events (3), Theatre (4) and Fine Arts (6).","The items, their timings and the number of participants and accompanists are the same for all zones and for the National Youth Festival.","The Chief Organizer or Co-ordinator (Events) may reschedule and announce the programme in advance if there is a sudden development.","Teams perform in the order decided by a draw of lots by the organizers.","The contingent leaders must make sure that the team reports for each event at the time and in the order announced by the organizers.","Participants must bring their own musical instruments and any special items needed for an item. Accompanists, if needed, must be arranged by the participating team, up to the limits set for the item.","Pre-recorded music (tape, cassette and similar) is not allowed in Folk Dance, Classical Dance and Creative Dance.","The decision of the judges appointed for each event is final and binding on all. Participants should study the rules for each event carefully.","Cultural events (One Act Play, Skits, Mime, Group Song (Indian) and Fine Arts) must show the basic values of Indian culture. These are values towards the unity and integration of the country, integrity, truth, devotion, loyalty and similar values, with particular reference to Indian cultural heritage. Such values may help remove obscurantism, religious fanaticism, violence, superstition and fatalism.","A grace time is allowed on the maximum time of an item. A performer who goes beyond the grace time is disqualified. The grace time is printed in each item's rules."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Only bonafide students who are pursuing a full-time course of study in a college or P.G. department can take part.","A student must be below 25 years of age on 1 July of the academic year in which the youth festival is held.","Not more than 7 years may have passed since the student passed the examination that qualified the student for first admission to a degree or diploma course of a university or college.","A student can take part for one year more than the normal length of the academic programme that the student belongs to.","A student who is employed on a full-time basis is not eligible.","A participant who has performed three times in the Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival in solo items is not allowed to take part again. A certificate to this effect must be obtained from the team manager.","Participants must carry identity cards with a photograph, signed by the proper authority of their college or department.","If any participant of a team is found ineligible, the university may take suitable action against the member concerned, and the college or department team may be debarred from future Youth Festivals for one year."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register and Report",Items:["A college or P.G. department sends its team as a contingent. The college or department sends at most two persons as contingent-in-charge, who keep contact with the organizing committee of the university. Officials count in the contingent strength.","A college or department is encouraged to send a lady in-charge to go with the girl participants.","Three copies of a brief note on the theme of each item to be presented must be given to the Convenor of the university at least 3 days before the festival starts.","The script of One Act Play, Skit, Mime, Group Song, Monologue, Mono-acting and similar items must be approved in advance by the committee set up for this purpose. Send it to the university at least 5 days before the event starts.","A participant who cannot take part for a valid reason can be replaced by not more than two participants in Group Songs, Folk Dances and Theatre events. Tell the university well in advance, with a certificate or application authorised by the Principal or Head of Department.","Folk/Tribal Dance, Classical Dance and Creative Choreography need a brief note given at registration. See each item's rules."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries and Contingent",Items:["Each college or P.G. department may send only one entry in each item. The item rules print this for each item.","The most members of a contingent from one college or P.G. department is 49, counting participants, accompanists and officials. If the university takes part in Folk/Tribal Dance, the contingent may be at most 58.","At most 8 outsider accompanists are allowed. They count in the contingent strength. Accompanists should preferably be students, but outsiders may be allowed if suitable students are not available.","Student accompanists are given participation certificates.","The Events for Youth Festival table prints, for each item, the participants, the accompanists, the total (P + A) and the least and most time. The rules of each item repeat these limits."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Points and Championship",Items:["For all individual events: First place 5 points, Second place 3 points, Third place 1 point.","For all group events: First place 7 points, Second place 5 points, Third place 3 points.","Points for the General Championship are counted in an item only if at least five teams or participants (in individual items) actually took part in that item.","If fewer than five participants or teams took part, certificates for First, Second and Third position are still given to the winners."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Trophies and Certificates",Items:["A Running Trophy is given to the winning institute (General Championship).","A Running Trophy is given to the runners-up institute (General Runners-up).","Certificates for First and Second position are given in each item.","Winning a place in the festival does not mean the winning team gets a place in the university team for the inter-university competition. The final teams and items for the Inter-University Competition are chosen only by the judges or the University Selection Committee. The final decision rests with the university."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct, Protests and Discipline",Items:["All participants must keep the dignity and decorum of the festival at all times.","If a contingent behaves against the objectives of the festival, the university may take suitable action against the member concerned, and the college or department team may be debarred from future Youth Festivals for one year.","No member of a participating team, including unofficial members, may interfere with the running of the festival or any event. They must not argue with the supervising officials of the organizers and must not question the judgment of the judges.","A participating team has the right to lodge a written protest on any point on which it feels aggrieved. The procedure in the rules must then be followed strictly.","No official or participant of any college or department may go to the press on any controversial issue. A person who does this can be debarred from the Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival for a period the university decides."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27",Url:"https://www.spuvvn.edu/University_Section/Physical_Education/2026-27/Youth-Festival-HandBook-2026-27-1.pdf"}]},a=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Handbook, Rules and Regulation 16 and 7",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["First place 5 points, Second place 3 points, Third place 1 point."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- First place 5 points, Second place 3 points, Third place 1 point.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Handbook, Rules and Regulation 16 and 10",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["First place 7 points, Second place 5 points, Third place 3 points."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- First place 7 points, Second place 5 points, Third place 3 points.`}],i=[],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Classical Vocal Solo (Hindustani or Karnatik)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Classical Vocal Solo and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).","Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.","The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes for each style.","A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style.","Choose the raga and the composition with sufficient thought and care."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Cinema songs are not allowed in this item."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities like Swar, Tal, selection of Raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).\\n- Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.\\n- The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes for each style.\\n- A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style.\\n- Choose the raga and the composition with sufficient thought and care.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Cinema songs are not allowed in this item.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities like Swar, Tal, selection of Raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion Tal Vadya) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).","Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.","The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes.","A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","Participants must bring their own instruments.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is most likely based on qualities like Tal, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).\\n- Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.\\n- The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is most likely based on qualities like Tal, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion, Swar Vadya) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).","Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.","The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes.","A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","Participants must bring their own instruments.","The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style."],"Allowed":["Instruments of western origin that are adapted to the Indian Raga system are allowed."],"NotAllowed":["Casio (an electronic keyboard) is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judgment is most likely based on qualities like Swar, Tal, selection of Raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).\\n- Time for setting is at most 5 minutes.\\n- The item lasts at least 8 minutes and at most 10 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 30 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatik style.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Instruments of western origin that are adapted to the Indian Raga system are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Casio (an electronic keyboard) is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is most likely based on qualities like Swar, Tal, selection of Raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Light Vocal (Indian)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Light Vocal (Indian) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One vocalist and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).","Time for setting is at most 2 minutes.","The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one vocalist per college or department is allowed."],"Allowed":["Only non-film songs can be presented: Geet, Ghazal, Bhajan, Shabad and Abhanga."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is made on qualities like Swar, Tal, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One vocalist and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).\\n- Time for setting is at most 2 minutes.\\n- The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one vocalist per college or department is allowed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only non-film songs can be presented: Geet, Ghazal, Bhajan, Shabad and Abhanga.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is made on qualities like Swar, Tal, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Western Vocal Solo and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).","Time for setting is at most 2 minutes.","The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The language of the song can only be English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is made on qualities like composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 2 accompanists (3 people in all).\\n- Time for setting is at most 2 minutes.\\n- The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The language of the song can only be English.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is made on qualities like composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."},{"Title":"Group Song (Indian)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Group Song (Indian) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 6 singers and at most 3 accompanists who play instruments (9 people in all).","The group song can last at most 10 minutes, not counting setting time.","Setting time for a group is at most 4 minutes.","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The same team presents two group songs. One is a folk song and the other is a patriotic song.","The songs must be Indian songs, in any regional language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No film song may be presented as a group song."],"Judging":["Judging is based on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 6 singers and at most 3 accompanists who play instruments (9 people in all).\\n- The group song can last at most 10 minutes, not counting setting time.\\n- Setting time for a group is at most 4 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The same team presents two group songs. One is a folk song and the other is a patriotic song.\\n- The songs must be Indian songs, in any regional language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No film song may be presented as a group song.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Group Song (Western)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Group Song (Western) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 6 singers and at most 3 accompanists who play instruments (9 people in all).","The group song can last at most 10 minutes, not counting setting time.","Setting time for a group is at most 5 minutes.","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The songs must be in the English language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is based on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 6 singers and at most 3 accompanists who play instruments (9 people in all).\\n- The group song can last at most 10 minutes, not counting setting time.\\n- Setting time for a group is at most 5 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The songs must be in the English language.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on the quality of singing only, not on make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Folk Orchestra and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The events table prints 9 participants and 3 accompanists (12 people in all); the item rules say the team has up to 12 participants.","The performance lasts at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).","Setting time is at most 5 minutes and is not counted in the performance time."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The group can be all boys, all girls or a mix.","Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They must wear different dress from the student participants so that they can be easily identified.","The accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team.","The team should preferably present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The events table prints 9 participants and 3 accompanists (12 people in all); the item rules say the team has up to 12 participants.\\n- The performance lasts at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).\\n- Setting time is at most 5 minutes and is not counted in the performance time.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The group can be all boys, all girls or a mix.\\n- Up to three professional accompanists are allowed. They must wear different dress from the student participants so that they can be easily identified.\\n- The accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team.\\n- The team should preferably present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs."},{"Title":"Western Instrumental Solo","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Western Instrumental Solo and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 3 accompanists (4 people in all).","The performance lasts between 6 and 8 minutes.","Time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per university is allowed.","The participant performs Western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.","The participant may perform in any one genre or style, or fuse several genres or styles of Western music."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music, musical patches and presets from keyboards are not allowed. The accompaniment must be live."],"Judging":["The performance is judged on Technical Proficiency, Musicianship and Dynamics, Rhythmic Accuracy and Timing, Selection and Arrangement, and Overall Impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 3 accompanists (4 people in all).\\n- The performance lasts between 6 and 8 minutes.\\n- Time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per university is allowed.\\n- The participant performs Western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.\\n- The participant may perform in any one genre or style, or fuse several genres or styles of Western music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music, musical patches and presets from keyboards are not allowed. The accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The performance is judged on Technical Proficiency, Musicianship and Dynamics, Rhythmic Accuracy and Timing, Selection and Arrangement, and Overall Impact."},{"Title":"Folk/Tribal Dance","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Folk/Tribal Dance (Indian) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 10 participants and 5 accompanists (15 people in all).","The dance lasts at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.","Time for setting the sets and instruments is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix.","The dance can be a primitive dance or a folk dance (Indian style).","Three copies of a brief note giving the theme and the text of the song, if any, are submitted with the entry form at registration.","The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["A classical dance is not allowed in this item.","Pre-recorded music such as tape and cassette is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on Rhythm, Formation, Expression, Costumes, Make-up, Sets and Overall Effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 10 participants and 5 accompanists (15 people in all).\\n- The dance lasts at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n- Time for setting the sets and instruments is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The team can be all boys, all girls or a mix.\\n- The dance can be a primitive dance or a folk dance (Indian style).\\n- Three copies of a brief note giving the theme and the text of the song, if any, are submitted with the entry form at registration.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A classical dance is not allowed in this item.\\n- Pre-recorded music such as tape and cassette is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on Rhythm, Formation, Expression, Costumes, Make-up, Sets and Overall Effect."},{"Title":"Classical Dance (Indian)","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Classical Dance (Indian) and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to 3 accompanists (4 people in all).","Each participant is allowed up to 15 minutes, including time for preparation and exit (the events table prints a minimum of 12 minutes).","The performer is disqualified after the maximum grace time."],"Rules":["Each college or department can send only one entry.","A participant can present a dance from any approved school of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam and Odissi.","Three copies of a brief note are submitted at registration. The note describes the story of the dance, if any, and gives the accompanying song, if any, with its meaning in Hindi or English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Pre-recorded music such as tape and cassette is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judgment is based mainly on Tal and Technique, Rhythm, Abhinaya or expression, Costumes, Footwork and General Impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to 3 accompanists (4 people in all).\\n- Each participant is allowed up to 15 minutes, including time for preparation and exit (the events table prints a minimum of 12 minutes).\\n- The performer is disqualified after the maximum grace time.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each college or department can send only one entry.\\n- A participant can present a dance from any approved school of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam and Odissi.\\n- Three copies of a brief note are submitted at registration. The note describes the story of the dance, if any, and gives the accompanying song, if any, with its meaning in Hindi or English.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pre-recorded music such as tape and cassette is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based mainly on Tal and Technique, Rhythm, Abhinaya or expression, Costumes, Footwork and General Impression."},{"Title":"Creative Choreography","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Creative Choreography and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 12 participants and 3 accompanists (15 people in all).","The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","Time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per university is allowed.","The performance must show a clear theme or message through dance. It can use a single dance form or style or a fusion of many.","The theme should be suitable for public viewing. It should preferably be youth-centric, nation-centric or about social issues.","Teams must bring or arrange their own props, if any.","Three copies of a brief note describing the theme are submitted with the entry form at registration. The note should be in Hindi or English only and may preferably be given at the registration or reporting desk of the venue.","Up to three accompanists are allowed. They may help with props, technical cues, background narration or effects. They stay off-stage, may be seen for a moment while doing these tasks, and are not part of the performance."],"Allowed":["Recorded music is allowed. Teams must take care in choosing songs so that the essence and spirit of the Youth Festival are kept."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Choreography is judged on theme and message clarity, choreography and creativity, synchronization and coordination, use of stage and props, costumes and overall impact.","Extra effort to improve the look of the performance through set design is not counted for marking."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 12 participants and 3 accompanists (15 people in all).\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per university is allowed.\\n- The performance must show a clear theme or message through dance. It can use a single dance form or style or a fusion of many.\\n- The theme should be suitable for public viewing. It should preferably be youth-centric, nation-centric or about social issues.\\n- Teams must bring or arrange their own props, if any.\\n- Three copies of a brief note describing the theme are submitted with the entry form at registration. The note should be in Hindi or English only and may preferably be given at the registration or reporting desk of the venue.\\n- Up to three accompanists are allowed. They may help with props, technical cues, background narration or effects. They stay off-stage, may be seen for a moment while doing these tasks, and are not part of the performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Recorded music is allowed. Teams must take care in choosing songs so that the essence and spirit of the Youth Festival are kept.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Choreography is judged on theme and message clarity, choreography and creativity, synchronization and coordination, use of stage and props, costumes and overall impact.\\n- Extra effort to improve the look of the performance through set design is not counted for marking."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Quiz and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each college or department can send a team of three persons.","There is a written preliminary round and teams are selected for the finals.","The finals are oral and may also have audio-visual questions."],"Rules":["The specific rules for evaluation, the time to reply and the type of round are given before the competition starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each college or department can send a team of three persons.\\n- There is a written preliminary round and teams are selected for the finals.\\n- The finals are oral and may also have audio-visual questions.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The specific rules for evaluation, the time to reply and the type of round are given before the competition starts."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Elocution and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant. Each participant has at most 5 minutes.","A warning bell rings at the end of 4 minutes.","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes)."],"Rules":["Each college or department nominates only one participant.","The language of presentation is Hindi or English.","The topic is told 24 hours in advance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant. Each participant has at most 5 minutes.\\n- A warning bell rings at the end of 4 minutes.\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each college or department nominates only one participant.\\n- The language of presentation is Hindi or English.\\n- The topic is told 24 hours in advance."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Debate and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each debater can speak for at most 5 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes)."],"Rules":["Each college or department is represented by two debaters. One speaks for the motion and the other speaks against it.","The medium of expression is Hindi or English.","The topic is told 24 hours in advance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each debater can speak for at most 5 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each college or department is represented by two debaters. One speaks for the motion and the other speaks against it.\\n- The medium of expression is Hindi or English.\\n- The topic is told 24 hours in advance."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, One Act Play and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 9 participants and 3 accompanists (12 people in all).","The play lasts at most 30 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 25 minutes).","A grace time of at most 45 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.","Time is counted as soon as the signal is given or the team starts giving the introduction, whichever is earlier.","Empty stage to empty stage must be followed strictly. Up to 10 minutes are given for stage setting and removal of sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage.","The team must report to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation."],"Rules":["Only one entry is accepted from each college or department.","The team brings its own set and stage properties, make-up material and so on. Light and general properties may be provided on advance information.","The play can be in Hindi, English or any regional language of India.","If the language is a regional language other than Gujarati, give the in-charge of the competition a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi. Give it 3 days before the event starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is most likely based on qualities of the play like theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 9 participants and 3 accompanists (12 people in all).\\n- The play lasts at most 30 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 25 minutes).\\n- A grace time of at most 45 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performer is disqualified.\\n- Time is counted as soon as the signal is given or the team starts giving the introduction, whichever is earlier.\\n- Empty stage to empty stage must be followed strictly. Up to 10 minutes are given for stage setting and removal of sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage.\\n- The team must report to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry is accepted from each college or department.\\n- The team brings its own set and stage properties, make-up material and so on. Light and general properties may be provided on advance information.\\n- The play can be in Hindi, English or any regional language of India.\\n- If the language is a regional language other than Gujarati, give the in-charge of the competition a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi. Give it 3 days before the event starts.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is most likely based on qualities of the play like theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."},{"Title":"Skits","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Skits and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["At most 6 participants and 3 accompanists (9 people in all).","Each team is given at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).","A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performers are disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed.","The team gives three copies of the names of the participants, with the language of presentation, at least 2 hours before the presentation."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not allowed.","Vulgarity and bitter insinuations should be avoided."],"Judging":["The item is judged basically on qualities like theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- At most 6 participants and 3 accompanists (9 people in all).\\n- Each team is given at most 10 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 8 minutes).\\n- A grace time of at most 15 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performers are disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n- The team gives three copies of the names of the participants, with the language of presentation, at least 2 hours before the presentation.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not allowed.\\n- Vulgarity and bitter insinuations should be avoided.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The item is judged basically on qualities like theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Mime and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":["Mukabhinaya or Mime is acting without words. It expresses ideas and themes, or tells a story, through gestures, postures, facial expressions and physical movement only. A mime actor does not need any object or stage property for acting.","Good power of observation, imagination, sense of time, variation of movements, style of presentation and theme can give a very good Mime performance."],"TimeAndFormat":["At most 6 participants and 2 accompanists (8 people in all).","Each team is given at most 5 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes).","A grace time of at most 5 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performers are disqualified."],"Rules":["Only one entry per college or department is allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is most likely based on qualities like idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, costume, music and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Mukabhinaya or Mime is acting without words. It expresses ideas and themes, or tells a story, through gestures, postures, facial expressions and physical movement only. A mime actor does not need any object or stage property for acting.\\n- Good power of observation, imagination, sense of time, variation of movements, style of presentation and theme can give a very good Mime performance.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- At most 6 participants and 2 accompanists (8 people in all).\\n- Each team is given at most 5 minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes).\\n- A grace time of at most 5 seconds is allowed. After the grace time, the performers are disqualified.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per college or department is allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is most likely based on qualities like idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, costume, music and general impression."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Mimicry and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant. Each student artist is given five minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes)."],"Rules":["Only one entry from the college or department is allowed."],"Allowed":["Participants may mimic the sound of machines and the speech of well-known persons, including film personalities."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Marking is based on skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant. Each student artist is given five minutes (the events table prints a minimum of 4 minutes).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry from the college or department is allowed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants may mimic the sound of machines and the speech of well-known persons, including film personalities.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Marking is based on skill in imitating, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."},{"Title":"On The Spot Painting","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, On the Spot Painting and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The item is held on the spot, on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The painting is on half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches by 15 inches.","The university gives only the paper or sheet. Candidates bring their own materials such as brushes and paints."],"Allowed":["The painting can be done in oil, water, poster or pastel colours."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The item is held on the spot, on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The painting is on half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches by 15 inches.\\n- The university gives only the paper or sheet. Candidates bring their own materials such as brushes and paints.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The painting can be done in oil, water, poster or pastel colours."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Collage and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The item is held on the spot. The participant makes a collage on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The university gives the material for the collage, such as paper and magazines or journals.","Participants bring their own scissors, adhesive and other material they need for the contest."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The item is held on the spot. The participant makes a collage on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The university gives the material for the collage, such as paper and magazines or journals.\\n- Participants bring their own scissors, adhesive and other material they need for the contest."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Poster Making and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The item is held on the spot. The participant makes a poster on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Candidates bring their own materials such as brushes and colours.","The university gives only the paper or sheet."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The item is held on the spot. The participant makes a poster on a subject given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Candidates bring their own materials such as brushes and colours.\\n- The university gives only the paper or sheet."},{"Title":"Clay Modeling","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Clay Modelling and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The item is held on the spot.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The university gives the clay.","Topics and other specific rules are announced on the spot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The item is held on the spot.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The university gives the clay.\\n- Topics and other specific rules are announced on the spot."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Cartooning and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The item is held on the spot, on the given subject or idea.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The handbook's rule on what participants bring is cut off in the printed copy (it reads only \\"Participants shall bring their\\")."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The item is held on the spot, on the given subject or idea.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The handbook's rule on what participants bring is cut off in the printed copy (it reads only \\"Participants shall bring their\\")."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Handbook of Rules and Regulations 2026-27, Rangoli and Handbook, Events for Youth Festival table","Sections":{"About":["This art is known by different names in different regions, such as Mandana, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli."],"TimeAndFormat":["One participant from each college or department.","The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The participant brings the required material.","The medium and form of expression can be free hand, pictorial or descriptive.","The participant prepares the rangoli within the space provided by the university."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This art is known by different names in different regions, such as Mandana, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- One participant from each college or department.\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participant brings the required material.\\n- The medium and form of expression can be free hand, pictorial or descriptive.\\n- The participant prepares the rangoli within the space provided by the university."}]`),s=[],r=[],l=[{Claim:"Rules, eligibility, contingent size, points, trophies, protests and every item's rules were read from the university's own handbook.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Sardar Patel University Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival Hand Book 2026-27",Url:"https://www.spuvvn.edu/University_Section/Physical_Education/2026-27/Youth-Festival-HandBook-2026-27-1.pdf"}],m={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,d as Year,m as default};
